// ADR-107 round 5, ADR-111: the copy of the guided tours (ui-tour.js, steps in ui-tour-steps.js) in every production language. An Options-only
// module, like fingerprint-identity-labels.js: the shared locale tables (and so background.js, popup.js, sidepanel.js and report.js) stay unchanged.
// Placeholders: {n} {total} {title}, replaced by the UI (never "$"). The texts name no button; they name a section only where the tour is about
// the sections themselves (the Control center, the Settings entry to Browser Debug, the two integrations), in the words the interface itself uses
// for it. They promise nothing about invisibility or coverage and say what is not covered. Direct quotation marks follow each
// language; the quoted step title is the title of another tour step. One table per language, in the order of the production languages.
// Every step id of every tour has a title and a text (step_<id>_title, step_<id>_body); the common keys carry the popover, the entry
// points and the header button (tour_label, tour_tip, tour_tip_resume).
